                <pb facs="0436" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/109: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica (Eberhardt) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-11-15T14:00:00-06:00">November 15,
                            1932—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. Minister Pacheco called to inform me
                    confidentially that principally to further his own prestige in Central America
                    he is endeavoring to secure permission from President Jiménez to proceed to Guatemala to confer with
                    President Ubico for the purpose of
                    calling a conference of emissaries from the co-signers of the 1923 Treaty of
                    Peace and Amity with a view to forthwith denouncing the treaty and recognizing
                    the Martínez régime.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
